│ patch_description        │ Remove the post-entanglement RZ layer. Every CZ gate is diagonal in the computational     │
│                          │ basis and therefore commutes with RZ rotations. Consequently, each post RZ can be moved   │
│                          │ across the CZ network and merged with the corresponding pre RZ, making nine parameters    │
│                          │ per block functionally redundant. Removing this layer preserves the effective hypothesis  │
│                          │ class while reducing the total parameter count from 162 to 108, lowering depth and gate   │
│                          │ count, and likely improving optimization speed, parameter efficiency, and generalization. │
