│ patch_name               │ remove_commuting_redundancy                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Remove the pre-entanglement RZ layer because every RZ commutes with the intervening CZ    │
│                          │ network, making the two RZ layers largely redundant and unnecessarily expensive. Convert  │
│                          │ the remaining post-entanglement rotations to RX so they do not commute with CZ. This      │
│                          │ yields a compact RY–CZ–RX hardware-efficient block, reducing the independent parameter    │
│                          │ count by one third while improving useful state mixing, circuit depth, convergence, and   │
│                          │ regularization.                                                                           │
