│ patch_description        │ Replace four well-distributed fixed CZ gates with trainable CRZ interactions, allowing    │
│                          │ the optimizer to tune entanglement strength across the connectivity graph. To offset      │
│                          │ their added parameters, tie each post-entanglement RZ angle to the corresponding          │
│                          │ pre-entanglement RZ angle. Because the intervening CZ/CRZ gates are diagonal in the       │
│                          │ computational basis, the pre/post RZ rotations are otherwise redundantly parameterized;   │
│                          │ tying them preserves the relevant accumulated local phase while reducing the total        │
│                          │ parameter count from 162 to 132. This should improve parameter efficiency and convergence │
│                          │ while adding useful entanglement flexibility.                                             │
