│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tied_noncommuting_sandwich                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the proven full CZ connectivity while correcting the main weakness of   │
│                          │ the current circuit: the repeated post-entanglement RZ layer commutes with CZ and         │
│                          │ therefore adds depth without useful noncommuting structure. The replacement uses a tied   │
│                          │ RY layer after entanglement, reusing the original per-wire RY parameters. This creates a  │
│                          │ genuinely noncommuting rotation–entanglement–rotation sandwich without increasing         │
│                          │ parameter count.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The RZ parameters are shared across mirrored wire pairs (0,8), (1,7), (2,6), and (3,5),   │
│                          │ with an independent center parameter for wire 4. This reduces each block from 18 to 14    │
│                          │ independent parameters while retaining wire-specific RY control, targeting better         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and generalization without discarding the connectivity that produced │
│                          │ the strongest prior validation result.                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
