│ patch_name               │ boundary_rx_hubs                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses nine independent RY parameters and nine shared RZ parameters      │
│                          │ repeated on both sides of the CZ network. Its duplicated commuting RZ layers increase     │
│                          │ depth without adding independent parameters, while the most connected boundary qubits, 0  │
│                          │ and 8, receive no noncommuting post-entanglement mixing. This revision replaces the       │
│                          │ initial RY gates on wires 0 and 8 with post-CZ RX rotations. The parameter count and gate │
│                          │ count remain unchanged, but the new RX parameters can transform entanglement-generated    │
│                          │ phase information into measurable population differences. Retaining independent rotations │
│                          │ elsewhere preserves local expressivity, while the focused boundary configuration avoids   │
│                          │ increasing model complexity or overfitting risk. Learning rate, iteration count, and      │
│                          │ convergence thresholds remain fixed by the external training loop.                        │
