│ patch_description        │ This ansatz returns to the shallower, fully fixed CZ interaction graph while introducing  │
│                          │ only moderate parameter sharing. The RY rotations on wires 1 and 7 share one parameter,   │
│                          │ and wires 2 and 6 share another; all remaining RY and RZ rotations stay independent. This │
│                          │ reduces the block from 18 to 16 unique parameters without sacrificing the phase           │
│                          │ flexibility that was lost under broader RZ sharing. Removing the extra repeated RZ layer  │
│                          │ and trainable CRZ gates also lowers depth, gate count, and overfitting pressure relative  │
│                          │ to the current 132-parameter circuit.                                                     │
