│ patch_description        │ This design preserves the proven 12-edge interaction graph while replacing only the two   │
│                          │ peripheral CZ links [1,8] and [4,8] with independently trainable CRZ gates. Unlike the    │
│                          │ earlier phase-sharing approach, it retains independent RZ parameters so each qubit can    │
│                          │ learn its own phase response. Regularization is instead applied selectively to the RY     │
│                          │ layer by sharing amplitudes across graph-related wire pairs (1,4), (2,3), and (5,6). This │
│                          │ reduces the parameter count relative to the current program while retaining independent   │
│                          │ rotations on the structurally distinct hub wires 0, 7, and 8. The result combines         │
│                          │ controlled peripheral adaptivity with axis-selective parameter sharing, aiming to reduce  │
│                          │ overfitting without sacrificing phase expressivity.                                       │
