│ patch_description        │ This design extends the strongest higher-order interaction pattern from the prior         │
│                          │ candidates into a complementary dual-hyperedge structure. It retains independent RY       │
│                          │ amplitudes and symmetry-shared RZ phases, then adds ZZZ interactions on [2,4,6] and       │
│                          │ [1,3,8] to model two distinct three-body correlations. To control depth and gate count,   │
│                          │ the less critical CZ edge [3,5] is removed. Thus, higher-order expressivity is increased  │
│                          │ without enlarging the per-block gate count relative to the single-ZZZ design.             │
