│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mid_rx_matching                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses six shared RY amplitudes, nine independent RZ phases, one         │
│                          │ trainable controlled phase, and three commuting CZ matching stages. Its main limitation   │
│                          │ is that the matching stages are nearly uninterrupted, restricting how phase correlations  │
│                          │ are converted into measurable amplitude information. The proposed circuit inserts a       │
│                          │ graph-symmetry-shared RX layer between the second and third matching stages. This         │
│                          │ introduces only six parameters per block while breaking the commuting entanglement        │
│                          │ sequence and enabling additional feature mixing. The underperforming CRZ hub is replaced  │
│                          │ with a fixed CZ, preserving the complete interaction graph while reducing unnecessary     │
│                          │ controlled-rotation capacity. This configuration targets higher validation accuracy and   │
│                          │ lower loss with substantially fewer parameters than the 180-parameter dual-output-layer   │
│                          │ program.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
