│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mid_rx_matching_mixer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Reorder the commuting CZ network into disjoint matchings and insert a symmetry-shared RX  │
│                          │ layer between the second and third matchings. The improved scheduling lowers entangling   │
│                          │ depth, while the noncommuting mid-circuit rotations prevent the entire CZ network from    │
│                          │ behaving like one phase-only layer. Sharing RX parameters across graph-related wires adds │
│                          │ only six independent parameters per block, providing a capacity increase smaller than a   │
│                          │ full independent rotation layer and helping preserve generalization and parameter         │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
