│ patch_description        │ This replaces the dense CZ sandwich with a hierarchical parity-phase network. A balanced  │
│                          │ CNOT tree gathers multi-qubit parity information onto intermediate nodes, trainable RZ    │
│                          │ and shared ZZZ interactions learn correlated phase features, and the reversed tree        │
│                          │ uncomputes the parity workspace. Tied input/output RY layers provide regularization while │
│                          │ retaining noncommuting transformations between repeated blocks. The design uses fewer     │
│                          │ parameters than the current ansatz, removes redundant all-edge entanglement, and should   │
│                          │ improve parameter efficiency and optimization stability.                                  │
