│ patch_name               │ tied_midpoint_reupload                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 30 independent parameters per repeated block: six shared input RY │
│                          │ parameters, nine input RZ parameters, six shared output RY parameters, and nine output RZ │
│                          │ parameters. Its strong validation accuracy and small generalization gap indicate that the │
│                          │ graph-matched CZ backbone and existing parameter sharing are effective, but all local     │
│                          │ basis changes occur only before or after entanglement.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new configuration inserts an RY–RZ basis-remixing layer after the second CZ matching. │
│                          │ This allows the final interaction layers to act on newly learned local bases rather than  │
│                          │ merely extending a commuting CZ sequence. To control parameter growth and preserve        │
│                          │ generalization, midpoint rotations share parameters across the same graph-related qubit   │
│                          │ groups used by the existing RY layers. Training settings such as learning rate and        │
│                          │ iteration count are fixed externally, so the principal optimization choices available     │
│                          │ here are gate placement, parameter sharing, depth, and entanglement structure.            │
