│ patch_description        │ Restore the stronger two-basis-layer structure while regularizing every rotation family   │
│                          │ with the same graph-orbit parameter tying. Adding endpoint RY rotations lets all qubits   │
│                          │ participate in amplitude mixing, replacing the CCRZ bottleneck with the two missing CZ    │
│                          │ edges restores the complete allowed interaction graph with fixed low-capacity             │
│                          │ entanglement, and a tied post-entanglement RY/RZ layer provides noncommuting              │
│                          │ readout-basis adaptation. This should improve validation accuracy and loss while using    │
│                          │ fewer parameters than the prior 180-parameter two-layer candidate.                        │
